      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Luminescent laparoscopy was performed in 51 cases for the assessment of the intestinal blood circulation. Sixteen examinations were performed in acute cholecystitis. Pseudo-negative result has been obtained in 4.5% of the 67 observations. The traditional technique of laparoscopy used with the same purpose in 113 examinations gave errors in 48.7%."},
